WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:02.336
[♪ theme music playing]

00:24.316 --> 00:26.944
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

00:29.029 --> 00:30.739
ALL CHARACTERS, PLACES,
ORGANIZATIONS, ETC. ARE FICTIONAL

00:30.822 --> 00:32.199
CHILD ACTORS WERE FILMED
WITH GUARDIANS PRESENT

00:32.282 --> 00:33.951
ANIMALS WERE FILMED
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE RULES

00:34.034 --> 00:35.035
EPISODE 10

00:35.118 --> 00:37.871
While presenting
the long-term service awards,

00:37.955 --> 00:41.708
I also counted the number of years
that I've worked here.

00:41.792 --> 00:46.713
I married into Myungsoondang at 18,
and now I'm 72.

00:46.797 --> 00:49.049
So, I've worked here for 54 years.

00:49.132 --> 00:50.342
[guests gasp, murmur]

00:50.425 --> 00:51.551
[Philnyun chuckles]

00:51.969 --> 00:53.762
It's nothing to be shocked about.

00:54.346 --> 00:55.847
Here, at Myungsoondang,

00:55.931 --> 00:59.810
there's a baker who's been here
one year longer than I have.

00:59.893 --> 01:04.481
Because of her, even at my age,
I can't be the most senior here.

01:04.564 --> 01:06.066
[guests laugh]

01:06.149 --> 01:07.484
EXECUTIVES

01:08.777 --> 01:10.237
CEO LEE SUNGWOO

01:10.320 --> 01:12.739
[Philnyun] ...is long enough for the world
to change many times.

01:13.699 --> 01:15.033
-Hello?
-Over that long time,

01:15.117 --> 01:16.535
Myungsoondang has been through...

01:16.618 --> 01:17.828
[Hangu] That's great to hear.

01:17.911 --> 01:20.330
I hope to see you soon. Bye.

01:21.623 --> 01:23.000
[line disconnects, line ringing]

01:23.083 --> 01:25.544
[Philnyun] However, if there's one thing
that doesn't change...

01:25.627 --> 01:29.423
Set up two more seats at the VIP table.
For Beauté Department Store's people.

01:29.798 --> 01:30.799
Thanks.

01:30.882 --> 01:32.217
[♪ dramatic, whimsical music playing]

01:33.176 --> 01:35.262
[Philnyun] I learned
from my late mother-in-law

01:35.345 --> 01:37.639
the spirit of care and sharing.

01:39.099 --> 01:40.559
[Miyeon] Hey, Jingyeong.

01:40.642 --> 01:43.645
You're getting prettier by the day.

01:44.313 --> 01:46.606
Are you seeing anyone these days?

01:46.690 --> 01:47.858
Gosh, no.

01:47.941 --> 01:49.151
What a coincidence.

01:49.234 --> 01:51.778
-Eungsoo is also single.
-Mom, stop it.

01:53.363 --> 01:56.366
There's no need to look far
when the right one might be close by.

01:56.450 --> 01:58.243
-Right?
-[Eungsoo mumbles, chuckles]

01:58.327 --> 02:01.163
[Miyeon chuckles]
There really is no need to look far.

02:01.246 --> 02:02.664
[Eungsoo] Mom, stop it.

02:03.081 --> 02:04.082
Seriously.

02:04.166 --> 02:05.167
[Miyeon] Okay, fine.

02:05.625 --> 02:06.626
Yes, sir.

02:07.210 --> 02:10.339
I think I can secure a unit
for the mayor of Yongdu soon.

02:10.797 --> 02:14.676
I may be able to retrieve the house
that was lost through the raffle.

02:14.760 --> 02:16.553
[♪ dramatic, whimsical music continues]

02:22.017 --> 02:24.227
[♪ dramatic sting, music fades]

02:27.356 --> 02:28.732
Mr. Baek.

02:33.278 --> 02:34.988
Thank you so much for coming.

02:35.072 --> 02:36.740
Come on in.

02:36.823 --> 02:38.241
Mr. Kim.

02:38.325 --> 02:40.077
What's your relationship with Ms. Yoo?

02:40.160 --> 02:41.870
[♪ dramatic sting]

02:43.121 --> 02:45.374
Are you two really married?

02:45.457 --> 02:47.334
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

02:47.417 --> 02:48.877
Well, the thing is...

02:50.337 --> 02:51.421
[gulps]

02:53.340 --> 02:54.383
[Jingyeong] Mr. Baek?

02:57.886 --> 03:00.222
I thought it might be you.

03:01.807 --> 03:03.058
What brings you here?

03:03.141 --> 03:05.477
[Jingyeong] Oh, I'm here on business.

03:06.019 --> 03:08.313
I have something to tell you.
Do you have time now?

03:13.276 --> 03:15.278
This is a bit urgent.

03:20.701 --> 03:22.035
Excuse us, Wooju.

03:22.119 --> 03:23.161
Sure.

03:23.245 --> 03:24.538
Shall we?

03:38.176 --> 03:39.177
[sighs in relief]

03:39.261 --> 03:40.720
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

03:50.439 --> 03:51.731
The two of them

03:52.691 --> 03:53.733
aren't married.

03:55.652 --> 03:57.529
Why are you looking so shocked?

03:57.612 --> 03:58.947
You overheard everything.

04:09.207 --> 04:10.917
[Philnyun] I was hoping to speak with you.

04:11.626 --> 04:14.754
Are you personally close to my Wooju?

04:15.630 --> 04:16.715
[hesitates]

04:17.966 --> 04:19.176
Yes.

04:19.259 --> 04:22.095
[Philnyun] Team Manager Kim Wooju
is my grandson. You know that, right?

04:22.179 --> 04:23.513
Yes, I know.

04:25.891 --> 04:27.309
You knew?

04:27.392 --> 04:28.769
Well...

04:30.812 --> 04:32.689
I know Wooju very well.

04:35.066 --> 04:36.735
Is Mr. Kim the man...

04:36.818 --> 04:37.861
That's right.

04:37.944 --> 04:40.071
He's the guy I told you
I had feelings for.

04:43.533 --> 04:45.160
What are you going to do now?

04:47.788 --> 04:50.749
If not married, the prize will be revoked.

04:50.832 --> 04:53.877
Also, they'll have to take
legal responsibility.

04:54.461 --> 04:56.671
[sighs softly] Is that so?

04:58.924 --> 05:00.592
I'm left with no choice, then.

05:01.051 --> 05:03.512
I have no choice but to reveal

05:03.595 --> 05:05.597
what that house is going to be used for.

05:05.680 --> 05:08.767
Coincidentally, I also heard something.

05:12.229 --> 05:13.647
[♪ dramatic sting]

05:17.734 --> 05:20.320
[Jingyeong] Thank you for lending me
some clothes last time.

05:20.862 --> 05:22.781
I'm leaving them in front of your house.

05:22.864 --> 05:24.366
From Yoon Jingyeong.

05:29.538 --> 05:30.622
[sighs]

05:39.923 --> 05:40.966
[car approaching]

05:45.220 --> 05:46.888
[car door opens, closes]

05:51.393 --> 05:52.435
[mayor sighs]

05:54.062 --> 05:55.105
[car door closes]

05:55.397 --> 05:57.899
Give me a unit at Beauté Palace,

05:57.983 --> 06:01.319
and you won't have to worry
about the permit for the new store.

06:01.403 --> 06:03.280
It's all about helping each other.

06:03.363 --> 06:05.532
Of course, thank you
for looking out for me.

06:05.615 --> 06:06.700
[mayor chuckles]

06:07.909 --> 06:10.912
The air today is so crisp and fresh.

06:10.996 --> 06:12.622
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

06:19.379 --> 06:21.423
[Jingyeong] I had my windows open
at the time,

06:22.382 --> 06:24.593
so the conversation
was recorded on my dash cam.

06:24.676 --> 06:26.344
I downloaded it to my phone.

06:27.345 --> 06:28.471
Are you blackmailing me?

06:28.555 --> 06:30.390
I'm merely suggesting a deal.

06:31.308 --> 06:33.101
I get to protect my man.

06:33.184 --> 06:36.980
And you, Director, get to protect
whatever you need to protect.

06:37.814 --> 06:39.441
So, let's help each other.

06:43.612 --> 06:46.281
-[video game gunfire plays on tablet]
-[zombie snarls]

06:47.866 --> 06:49.534
-[rapid gunfire]
-[defeat chime]

06:50.160 --> 06:51.202
[sighs]

06:51.328 --> 06:52.329
Oh, right.

06:52.871 --> 06:54.122
What did you mean before?

06:54.831 --> 06:55.915
Retrieving the prize?

06:57.167 --> 06:58.501
Oh, that.

06:59.127 --> 07:01.129
Even if you reveal their fake marriage,

07:01.212 --> 07:02.881
isn't it a bigger deal for you

07:02.964 --> 07:04.841
if people found out about the bribe?

07:05.467 --> 07:06.968
I was mistaken.

07:07.427 --> 07:09.429
-What?
-I looked into it again,

07:10.221 --> 07:11.640
and there wasn't a way.

07:11.723 --> 07:13.266
What the heck?

07:14.309 --> 07:17.437
Hey, do you think I have time
to listen to your crap?

07:18.063 --> 07:19.522
Tell me only when you're sure.

07:20.106 --> 07:21.191
My apologies, sir.

07:23.943 --> 07:25.904
By the way, was it David?

07:25.987 --> 07:27.614
The one who worked at the Kaltz.

07:28.281 --> 07:29.532
Your acquaintance.

07:29.616 --> 07:30.617
Yes.

07:31.868 --> 07:33.453
He's a total nutcase.

07:33.536 --> 07:35.914
He sent a wreath bearing the hotel's name.

07:42.545 --> 07:44.172
[Hangu] Thank you for coming.

07:44.255 --> 07:45.507
Of course.

07:45.590 --> 07:47.634
1 HOUR AGO

07:49.969 --> 07:52.013
MANAGING DIRECTOR OF KALTZ HOTEL
David Lee

07:52.097 --> 07:53.431
[Sungwoo] David?

07:54.057 --> 07:55.433
Didn't he quit the hotel?

07:55.517 --> 07:57.268
[♪ tense music playing]

07:58.186 --> 07:59.312
[chuckles nervously] Oh, no.

07:59.396 --> 08:00.980
You must be mistaken.

08:02.649 --> 08:03.692
No, I'm sure.

08:04.359 --> 08:07.612
He said on the flight
that he quit the Kaltz Hotel.

08:07.696 --> 08:09.572
You must've misunderstood him.

08:15.328 --> 08:17.789
-Look into Director David Lee.
-[Juhee] Yes, ma'am.

08:21.251 --> 08:22.377
[door closes, beeps]

08:22.794 --> 08:24.337
Mr. Baek? Why?

08:24.796 --> 08:25.797
I'm not sure.

08:25.880 --> 08:27.716
He suddenly asked
if we were indeed married.

08:27.799 --> 08:29.801
But then, Jingyeong showed up.

08:29.884 --> 08:32.220
And I haven't heard from him since.

08:32.303 --> 08:33.763
I wonder what that was about.

08:34.389 --> 08:35.390
Wait.

08:35.473 --> 08:37.600
Do Mr. Baek and Jingyeong know each other?

08:38.309 --> 08:40.019
Apparently, they're in the same club.

08:40.103 --> 08:41.855
But I didn't know this until today.

08:42.856 --> 08:43.857
We'll be okay, right?

08:43.940 --> 08:45.400
We'll be okay.

08:45.817 --> 08:49.821
Even if he had his doubts,
Jingyeong would've handled it well.

08:49.904 --> 08:53.616
[sighs] I'm really being
a nuisance to Jingyeong.

08:54.284 --> 08:58.997
[sighs wearily] Anyway, I really wanted
to introduce you to my grandma today.

08:59.998 --> 09:02.292
I'll set up an appointment
tomorrow at the office.

09:03.460 --> 09:06.379
Oh, and we can meet
with Mr. Baek in the evening.

09:07.213 --> 09:10.050
I'm nervous
now that I'm actually about to do this.

09:10.550 --> 09:11.551
[chuckles softly]

09:15.096 --> 09:17.182
We said we'd face this together.

09:17.265 --> 09:18.391
So, don't worry.

09:18.475 --> 09:20.018
[♪ upbeat dreamy music playing]

09:21.519 --> 09:22.687
[sighs]

10:20.328 --> 10:21.579
[doorbell chimes]

10:33.424 --> 10:35.927
What a surprise.
You didn't even call first.

10:36.010 --> 10:37.595
When did you get back from the US?

10:38.888 --> 10:41.266
I came back last weekend.

10:41.349 --> 10:43.643
After staying in Yeosu for three days,

10:43.726 --> 10:47.689
I realized
that I don't get along with Mom.

10:48.481 --> 10:51.359
I have to get a job in Seoul, anyway.

10:51.442 --> 10:53.736
So, I was thinking
about staying at your house.

10:54.195 --> 10:55.780
I heard about the prize from Mom...

10:55.864 --> 10:56.865
[gasps] Oh, my.

10:58.158 --> 10:59.492
Who's this?

11:00.827 --> 11:02.412
Oh, this is...

11:02.996 --> 11:04.581
[in English] Just a moment.

11:04.831 --> 11:06.291
[♪ gripping, whimsical music playing]

11:14.340 --> 11:15.383
Hello.

11:15.967 --> 11:16.968
[Sori in Korean] Who's that?

11:17.468 --> 11:18.678
[Youngsook] What do you mean?

11:18.761 --> 11:20.805
It's Wooju, Kim Wooju.

11:20.889 --> 11:22.682
You're Kim Wooju, right?

11:23.141 --> 11:25.894
Yes, nice to meet you.
[chuckles sheepishly]

11:32.025 --> 11:33.234
[clears throat]

11:33.318 --> 11:34.402
Pass.

11:35.153 --> 11:37.155
-Pardon?
-Who are you to give him a pass?

11:37.238 --> 11:38.531
Gosh, you.

11:38.615 --> 11:40.575
Aren't you lucky this year?

11:41.701 --> 11:44.495
My girl here may not be sweet,
but she is genuine.

11:44.579 --> 11:46.456
So, please treat her well.

11:46.539 --> 11:47.582
Cut it out.

11:47.665 --> 11:48.791
Just be quiet.

11:48.875 --> 11:50.043
You be quiet.

11:50.126 --> 11:52.295
Or I'll tell him all about your temper.

11:53.087 --> 11:54.839
-[chuckles nervously]
-[Kim Wooju chuckles softly]

11:54.923 --> 11:57.842
I'll get going now
since your sister is here.

11:57.926 --> 11:59.135
[Sori] No, stay.

11:59.219 --> 12:01.721
Don't worry about me
and continue what you were doing.

12:02.639 --> 12:05.808
I'll quietly find myself
a spare room and sleep.

12:05.892 --> 12:08.228
I was on my way out, anyway.
[chuckles sheepishly]

12:08.311 --> 12:09.312
[Sori] Oh, gosh.

12:10.521 --> 12:11.981
I don't think you were.

12:13.066 --> 12:14.067
Right there.

12:14.692 --> 12:16.778
Your lips are telling me the truth.

12:16.861 --> 12:17.946
What?

12:19.280 --> 12:21.074
[♪ enthralling orchestral music playing]

12:24.661 --> 12:25.787
[Kim Wooju chuckles awkwardly]

12:25.870 --> 12:27.163
I'll get going then.

12:28.081 --> 12:29.624
-[mouthing] You're dead.
-[Kim Wooju] Bye.

12:31.459 --> 12:32.752
[Sori] Oh, my.

12:32.835 --> 12:35.213
Is the air conditioning really on?

12:35.797 --> 12:37.799
It feels a little heated in here.

12:37.882 --> 12:39.467
It's so hot.

12:45.306 --> 12:47.475
Geez, what's with her?

12:47.558 --> 12:49.519
You must be flustered. I'm sorry.

12:49.602 --> 12:51.354
Not at all, that was very cute of her.

12:51.938 --> 12:54.482
But I don't think she's very keen on me.

12:54.565 --> 12:56.150
What do you mean?

12:56.234 --> 12:57.777
Don't worry about her.

12:57.860 --> 12:59.988
Tell her that I'll treat her
to a good meal.

13:00.071 --> 13:01.072
I should win some points.

13:02.073 --> 13:03.074
Bye.

13:04.867 --> 13:06.536
[♪ whimsical music playing]

13:18.381 --> 13:19.424
I'll get going.

13:34.439 --> 13:37.358
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

13:47.410 --> 13:48.411
[Hangu sighs]

13:50.913 --> 13:52.415
[♪ ominous music playing]

13:58.212 --> 14:00.131
Look into Director David Lee.

14:00.715 --> 14:01.716
[Juhee] Yes, ma'am.

14:08.681 --> 14:10.224
[exhales deeply]

14:14.103 --> 14:15.104
[laughs slyly]

14:24.405 --> 14:25.782
[sighs]

14:26.783 --> 14:27.867
CHAIRWOMAN

14:28.367 --> 14:29.535
[line ringing]

14:31.621 --> 14:32.747
[line connects]

14:33.790 --> 14:35.583
Ma'am, it's Hangu.

14:35.666 --> 14:37.835
I have something important to tell you.

14:37.919 --> 14:38.920
What?

14:39.003 --> 14:40.088
The Kaltz Hotel said

14:40.171 --> 14:42.215
they've never had a contract with us.

14:42.924 --> 14:44.926
Nor have they ever reviewed a contract.

14:45.843 --> 14:48.679
I think we've been deceived
by Director David Lee.

14:48.763 --> 14:50.306
What do you mean?

14:50.765 --> 14:52.141
That contract was signed long ago!

14:53.059 --> 14:54.560
Call David now.

14:54.644 --> 14:56.938
No, I'll go to the US myself.

14:57.021 --> 14:59.148
I need to meet
with the CEO of Kaltz Hotel.

14:59.774 --> 15:01.359
[gasps] Ma'am.

15:05.321 --> 15:07.031
[breathing heavily]

15:12.578 --> 15:13.830
[bottle, pills clatter on floor]

15:13.913 --> 15:15.206
[breathing heavily]

15:16.332 --> 15:17.500
-[groans softly]
-Sit here.

15:18.292 --> 15:19.460
I'll get it for you.

15:19.544 --> 15:21.129
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

15:31.180 --> 15:33.099
-Here.
-[continues breathing heavily]

15:34.433 --> 15:35.726
[pills rattle in bottle]

15:37.562 --> 15:38.729
[sniffles]

15:47.446 --> 15:48.948
[continues breathing heavily]

15:49.031 --> 15:50.533
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

15:56.914 --> 15:59.375
Meeting the Kaltz Hotel people
wouldn't do any good.

16:01.210 --> 16:03.796
Because David was fired two years ago,

16:03.880 --> 16:06.299
they'll say
it's got nothing to do with them.

16:06.966 --> 16:08.676
[wheezing]

16:08.759 --> 16:09.886
Then?

16:10.595 --> 16:12.847
Are you telling me
to just stand by and watch?

16:13.681 --> 16:15.474
What about the plant in the US

16:16.309 --> 16:18.769
that cost us a fortune to build?

16:22.899 --> 16:24.817
You don't have to worry about that.

16:25.526 --> 16:27.945
The factory built
to supply the Kaltz Hotel...

16:30.573 --> 16:31.574
was fake.

16:31.657 --> 16:33.159
[♪ unsettling, tense music playing]

16:34.368 --> 16:38.331
We just rented an abandoned building
and did some simple Photoshop work.

16:38.831 --> 16:40.124
We never purchased the land.

16:45.630 --> 16:46.631
It was...

16:48.507 --> 16:49.884
all fake?

16:51.802 --> 16:52.845
Then,

16:53.971 --> 16:55.890
what about the money we've wired?

16:55.973 --> 16:58.893
If you've seen Mr. Ko's report,
you should've known

16:59.685 --> 17:01.562
that the money was siphoned off.

17:03.814 --> 17:07.568
Through J Consulting,
that money is now in my pocket.

17:09.237 --> 17:12.323
J Consulting is my company.

17:15.660 --> 17:16.869
[breath trembling]

17:20.456 --> 17:21.457
I...

17:22.625 --> 17:24.085
I had my doubts, but...

17:26.337 --> 17:27.421
Then, [sniffles]

17:28.130 --> 17:32.635
since David was introduced to us
through J Consulting,

17:34.011 --> 17:36.055
is the fake contract

17:37.515 --> 17:38.724
also your doing?

17:40.810 --> 17:41.811
That's right.

17:42.937 --> 17:44.730
Why would you do that?

17:45.690 --> 17:49.694
How are you going to face
Miyeon and Eungsoo?

17:50.069 --> 17:52.530
[hums thoughtfully]
I don't think I'll need to see them again.

17:52.613 --> 17:53.781
[laughs smugly]

17:54.657 --> 17:57.535
You should've just given me
a section of the company.

17:57.618 --> 17:59.704
After dumping your
pathetic daughter on me,

17:59.787 --> 18:02.081
have you had no conscience?
[clicks tongue]

18:02.164 --> 18:03.916
You only gave me a bit of inheritance,

18:04.000 --> 18:05.793
like I'm some beggar.
[clicks tongue]

18:05.876 --> 18:07.545
What? [wheezing]

18:07.878 --> 18:08.879
You...

18:09.589 --> 18:11.841
You bastard! [gasping, grunts]

18:15.136 --> 18:16.220
[thuds]

18:17.179 --> 18:18.639
[♪ music increases in tempo]

18:24.937 --> 18:26.564
[breathing heavily]

18:29.692 --> 18:31.444
The medicine's not working, is it?

18:34.113 --> 18:35.615
[♪ ominous sting]

18:40.786 --> 18:41.787
[sighs]

18:42.121 --> 18:43.456
[♪ ominous music playing]

18:53.549 --> 18:55.092
[Philnyun breathing heavily]

18:55.509 --> 18:57.178
[Hangu] You'll lose
your consciousness soon.

18:57.261 --> 19:00.139
Because of your chronic illness,
it'll be ruled as a natural death.

19:00.222 --> 19:02.141
Well, maybe it's for the best.

19:03.434 --> 19:05.019
Rather than seeing the company

19:05.102 --> 19:08.439
you gave your life to
get broken up and sold in pieces,

19:08.939 --> 19:10.775
isn't it better that you go before then?

19:10.858 --> 19:12.276
[wheezing]

19:16.947 --> 19:18.240
[Philnyun continues wheezing]

19:21.202 --> 19:22.411
[mumbles shakily]

19:24.080 --> 19:25.164
[gasps]

19:28.417 --> 19:30.044
[♪ music increases in tempo]

19:49.772 --> 19:51.524
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

19:53.401 --> 19:55.403
[♪ ominous sting]

19:57.154 --> 19:59.323
[Miyeon] Where is she?

20:00.366 --> 20:01.701
-Which room?
-Slow down.

20:01.784 --> 20:02.952
No one's picking up.

20:03.035 --> 20:04.829
[angrily] Why aren't they picking up
their phone?

20:04.912 --> 20:06.914
[Eungsoo] Seriously,
why aren't they picking up?

20:06.997 --> 20:08.833
-[Miyeon breathing heavily]
-Slow down.

20:10.000 --> 20:14.630
Luckily, she survived,
but she's barely responsive.

20:14.714 --> 20:16.716
The surgery went well,

20:16.799 --> 20:20.469
but because of her age
and chronic illness,

20:20.553 --> 20:23.681
at this point,
there's very little chance she'll wake up.

20:23.764 --> 20:28.102
Are you saying
Mom's just going to stay like this?

20:28.185 --> 20:29.770
She'll never wake up?

20:29.854 --> 20:32.940
When she came to the hospital,
she was already unconscious.

20:33.023 --> 20:34.692
[breath trembling]

20:36.485 --> 20:38.320
What were you doing, Ms. Kim?

20:38.404 --> 20:41.073
Where the hell were you,
leaving Mom all alone?

20:41.157 --> 20:42.450
What were you doing?

20:43.200 --> 20:44.702
I'm sorry. [sniffling]

20:45.119 --> 20:46.662
I was only out for a moment.

20:47.621 --> 20:48.622
Calm down.

20:48.706 --> 20:50.541
She's been ill for a while.

20:50.624 --> 20:52.334
[breathing heavily]

20:52.418 --> 20:55.755
She was fine
when I stopped by in the evening.

20:55.838 --> 20:57.381
[Miyeon] Oh, what do we do?

20:57.465 --> 20:59.467
What if my mom dies?

21:00.092 --> 21:01.427
Is there no other way

21:02.178 --> 21:04.138
than to just wait for her to wake up?

21:04.221 --> 21:06.515
[Dr. Yoon] Our priority is to stop
additional brain hemorrhage

21:06.599 --> 21:08.893
and to control her intracranial pressure.

21:09.518 --> 21:10.853
If bleeding reoccurs,

21:11.854 --> 21:12.855
she won't survive.

21:13.230 --> 21:14.315
[sighs]

21:14.982 --> 21:17.151
[Miyeon sobbing] Oh, no. Mom...

21:17.234 --> 21:18.986
[♪ tense, melancholy music playing]

21:19.111 --> 21:20.237
Mom...

21:25.034 --> 21:26.619
[Miyeon continues sobbing]

21:38.380 --> 21:39.381
[sighs softly]

21:41.133 --> 21:42.176
[line ringing]

21:45.387 --> 21:47.139
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

21:47.223 --> 21:48.224
Let's begin.

21:50.810 --> 21:51.811
[line disconnects]

21:56.023 --> 21:57.358
[sighs in relief]

21:58.818 --> 22:01.362
[news anchor over TV] Myungsoondang,
a bakery with an 80-year history,

22:01.445 --> 22:04.031
is under suspicion
of having received a large investment

22:04.114 --> 22:07.034
from an investment firm
through a falsified supply contract.

22:07.117 --> 22:11.580
Using a fake supply contract
with the global hotel Kaltz as collateral,

22:11.664 --> 22:14.458
Myungsoondang reportedly obtained

22:14.542 --> 22:17.920
an investment of 30 billion won
from BQ Capital, a US-based firm.

22:18.003 --> 22:20.339
Myungsoondang won
the President's Award this year

22:20.422 --> 22:22.299
for its outstanding
social contributions...

22:24.134 --> 22:25.261
[Miyeon sighs deeply]

22:25.344 --> 22:28.430
Mom was deceived.
You know what she's like.

22:28.514 --> 22:31.308
She would never go astray.

22:31.392 --> 22:33.143
Forged a contract?

22:33.686 --> 22:34.895
-[breathing heavily] Geez.
-Mom...

22:36.313 --> 22:39.775
Shouldn't we catch this David guy first?

22:39.859 --> 22:44.029
We should request an investigation
to catch this guy so that...

22:44.113 --> 22:45.698
It's no use. [sighs]

22:46.907 --> 22:48.200
It's still a fact

22:48.284 --> 22:51.370
that the chairwoman obtained
the investment through a fake contract.

22:52.371 --> 22:55.791
[sighs] I should've tried harder
to stop her.

22:56.292 --> 22:57.918
But is it actually true?

22:59.169 --> 23:00.546
Ms. Kim said

23:01.130 --> 23:03.674
Grandma met with David up until recently.

23:04.174 --> 23:06.010
Wasn't it to discuss the supply plan?

23:07.761 --> 23:10.389
She met with him for a different reason.

23:11.056 --> 23:12.683
To ask him to keep it a secret

23:12.766 --> 23:15.144
from the investors
that the contract was put on hold.

23:15.227 --> 23:16.604
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

23:16.687 --> 23:17.771
[Hangu sighs softly]

23:21.191 --> 23:23.068
MARKETING TEAM

23:23.152 --> 23:25.821
[Hangu] In her first year as Chairwoman,

23:26.405 --> 23:28.449
our operating profit was cut in half.

23:29.450 --> 23:31.076
Revenue held steady,

23:31.827 --> 23:34.371
but turning all the part-timers
into full-time employees

23:34.455 --> 23:36.248
sent labor costs through the roof.

23:36.832 --> 23:39.209
And after losing the lawsuit
over the logistics hub,

23:39.293 --> 23:40.586
we sank deeper into deficit.

23:41.795 --> 23:45.507
By forging the Kaltz Hotel contract,
which was still being negotiated,

23:45.591 --> 23:47.593
she told me
to secure the investment first.

23:48.218 --> 23:50.054
By putting out the fire,

23:50.888 --> 23:54.141
I think she meant to get the contract
signed in the meantime.

23:54.975 --> 23:56.018
[sighs]

23:58.228 --> 23:59.229
All this time,

24:01.023 --> 24:03.275
she's been struggling on her own.

24:04.902 --> 24:06.487
MS. KIM

24:10.324 --> 24:11.492
[phone vibrating]

24:13.369 --> 24:15.746
[♪ soft jazz music playing in background]

24:20.584 --> 24:22.544
You could've just come to my office.

24:25.965 --> 24:28.175
I have something to tell you privately.

24:30.386 --> 24:35.599
The chairwoman probably didn't know
that the contract with the Kaltz was fake.

24:36.850 --> 24:37.893
What?

24:37.977 --> 24:39.186
The day she collapsed,

24:39.812 --> 24:42.314
she asked me to look into David.

24:43.273 --> 24:45.067
[♪ soft, melancholy music playing]

24:50.781 --> 24:52.533
[Juhee] If she knew
it was a fake contract,

24:52.992 --> 24:55.536
why would she ask me to look into him?

24:56.245 --> 24:58.205
She didn't even know he had been fired.

25:19.977 --> 25:21.478
[Philnyun] It doesn't feel right.

25:21.979 --> 25:26.442
I'd like you to look into it
without Director Jang knowing.

25:31.447 --> 25:32.448
Grandma.

25:33.115 --> 25:34.533
I'm afraid.

25:40.873 --> 25:42.499
I'm afraid that you were right.

25:45.252 --> 25:46.253
BULLETIN BOARD

25:47.880 --> 25:50.549
SO MUCH FOR BEING
A SOCIALLY RESPONSIBLE COMPANY

25:50.632 --> 25:52.301
[Songhee sighing]
It's getting really messy.

25:52.384 --> 25:54.720
People are already starting a boycott.

25:54.803 --> 25:56.221
RETURN THE PRESIDENT'S AWARD!

25:56.305 --> 25:57.890
[♪ melancholy music continues]

26:17.409 --> 26:18.535
Mr. Kim.

26:28.545 --> 26:30.506
Did you have dinner?

26:31.090 --> 26:33.592
[sighs wearily]
I don't have much appetite.

26:33.967 --> 26:36.345
Anyway, what brings you by?

26:36.428 --> 26:37.638
What do you think?

26:37.721 --> 26:40.682
-I came to hear you sigh.
-[chuckles softly]

26:41.725 --> 26:43.018
Seriously.

26:43.852 --> 26:47.981
When things are hard,
they say it helps to take three big sighs.

26:48.065 --> 26:49.108
Nonsense.

26:49.191 --> 26:50.901
I'm serious. Try it.

26:51.693 --> 26:52.694
Go on.

26:55.656 --> 26:56.698
[sighs]

26:57.157 --> 26:58.200
[sighs softly]

26:58.659 --> 27:00.202
You must be really concerned.

27:00.285 --> 27:01.829
[sighs, chuckles]

27:02.204 --> 27:04.164
I can tell from your sighs.

27:04.248 --> 27:05.415
[acknowledges]

27:05.666 --> 27:07.835
-[sighs]
-You feel a little bit better, right?

27:08.627 --> 27:09.628
Mmm-hmm.

27:09.711 --> 27:12.172
You can tell me about anything.

27:12.256 --> 27:16.260
I'll listen with one ear
and let it out the other.

27:19.805 --> 27:21.014
[hums thoughtfully]

27:22.599 --> 27:23.725
[clicks tongue]

27:29.731 --> 27:30.774
[sighs softly]

27:31.525 --> 27:32.526
[Meri in English] Okay.

27:33.193 --> 27:35.571
[Meri singing in Korean]
♪ I want to know ♪

27:35.654 --> 27:40.701
♪ Even the smallest things about you ♪

27:40.784 --> 27:43.036
♪ But for some reason ♪

27:43.120 --> 27:47.374
♪ You don't tell me ♪

27:48.083 --> 27:49.585
[♪ soft, gentle music playing]

27:51.461 --> 27:53.964
Gosh, if I were you, I would've told you.

27:55.132 --> 27:56.174
Fine, I will.

27:58.468 --> 28:00.262
-Shall we take a walk?
-Sure.

28:05.809 --> 28:08.478
So, you're suspicious
of your uncle right now, right?

28:09.479 --> 28:13.567
I had my doubts even when she asked me
to look into J Consulting.

28:15.235 --> 28:17.863
I couldn't even ask him.

28:17.946 --> 28:19.573
Of course not.

28:19.990 --> 28:23.243
You said he was like a father to you.

28:23.869 --> 28:26.580
It's not like there's solid proof yet.

28:27.039 --> 28:30.083
I just know that he's lying.

28:30.500 --> 28:32.294
Then you should reveal the truth.

28:33.337 --> 28:36.089
When someone you trust betrays you,

28:36.173 --> 28:37.549
at first,

28:37.633 --> 28:41.970
you start wondering why they lied to you.

28:42.054 --> 28:43.889
Then you start blaming yourself.

28:44.890 --> 28:47.517
You start wondering
what you've done wrong,

28:47.601 --> 28:49.478
and when it started going wrong.

28:50.270 --> 28:53.315
But if you think about it again,

28:53.398 --> 28:55.108
it's not because you did something.

28:55.901 --> 28:57.736
The person who betrayed you is at fault.

28:58.904 --> 29:01.949
So, if your uncle is lying
about something,

29:02.032 --> 29:03.367
you should reveal it.

29:04.910 --> 29:06.536
Before he does something worse.

29:08.956 --> 29:10.916
Aren't you going to save Myungsoondang?

29:10.999 --> 29:12.501
That's what the successor is for.

29:12.584 --> 29:13.961
No one else can do this but you.

29:16.797 --> 29:19.132
Don't think too much.

29:20.133 --> 29:22.386
Just do what you can do right now.

29:22.469 --> 29:24.179
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

29:25.973 --> 29:29.309
If someone gives you a hard time,
I won't stand for it.

29:29.393 --> 29:30.435
[chuckles]

29:39.403 --> 29:40.487
Thank you.

30:04.970 --> 30:08.181
[Meri] If someone gives you a hard time,
I won't stand for it.

30:43.884 --> 30:44.968
[sighs]

30:57.314 --> 30:58.982
[♪ soft jazz music
playing in background]

31:01.193 --> 31:02.194
You're here.

31:02.277 --> 31:03.945
Would you like the same drink?

31:04.029 --> 31:05.197
Yes, please.

31:05.280 --> 31:06.323
Okay.

31:14.414 --> 31:16.541
At least say hi.

31:17.501 --> 31:18.960
We do share a secret after all.

31:19.669 --> 31:21.588
Isn't it better
to pretend to be strangers?

31:21.671 --> 31:23.006
I'm sure that'd be better.

31:23.381 --> 31:25.008
You think so?

31:27.302 --> 31:30.138
Anyway, thank you
for accepting my suggestion.

31:30.222 --> 31:33.100
I'm still thinking about it.
Don't get ahead of yourself.

31:33.642 --> 31:35.519
Is your boss still pressuring you?

31:35.602 --> 31:38.396
Play him my recording,
then he won't say another word.

31:38.480 --> 31:40.315
Then he'll pull the hospital's funding.

31:40.982 --> 31:42.818
Wow, how petty.

31:42.901 --> 31:44.277
That's the world of business.

31:51.326 --> 31:52.327
I don't get it.

31:54.663 --> 31:56.706
Why are you going to such lengths?

31:57.165 --> 31:59.668
You said Mr. Kim
doesn't see you as a woman.

32:00.752 --> 32:01.878
Mr. Baek.

32:03.421 --> 32:05.674
You've never
truly liked someone, have you?

32:06.216 --> 32:08.301
You want them to do well.

32:08.844 --> 32:10.762
You want to protect them.

32:10.846 --> 32:12.681
You feel their pain as if it's your own.

32:13.431 --> 32:16.643
There's no reason behind it,
no matter how much you try to find one.

32:16.726 --> 32:18.061
It's an automatic response.

32:20.230 --> 32:22.482
Still, it's not like he'll even notice.

32:22.566 --> 32:24.734
Stop hitting me with the hard truth.

32:25.527 --> 32:28.238
Even if he doesn't notice,
it doesn't matter, okay?

32:33.326 --> 32:34.327
[sighs softly]

32:35.287 --> 32:36.830
I'm sorry if I offended you.

32:36.913 --> 32:40.417
Because you heard a thing about me,

32:41.501 --> 32:42.586
I got a bit...

32:43.795 --> 32:45.088
sensitive.

32:45.172 --> 32:46.214
[exclaims quizzically]

32:46.590 --> 32:47.757
Heard what?

32:49.885 --> 32:51.553
Did I hear something?

32:53.221 --> 32:54.723
I don't care. You sort it out.

32:55.974 --> 32:58.351
Hey, do it like you blackmailed
my dad into paying

32:58.435 --> 33:01.188
to send you abroad to study
because you took an exam for me.

33:01.271 --> 33:03.064
You used to be quick on your feet.

33:03.148 --> 33:05.108
Why have you lost your touch?

33:06.026 --> 33:07.944
Has life been a little too good for you?

33:10.405 --> 33:11.573
Nothing.

33:11.656 --> 33:15.535
You know, people aren't really
interested in how you've lived.

33:16.578 --> 33:19.998
So, stop acting all guilty like that.

33:20.081 --> 33:22.250
[stutters] I don't feel guilty.

33:22.334 --> 33:25.837
I think you do,
[mockingly] judging by your stutter.

33:26.630 --> 33:27.756
[chuckles softly]

33:28.506 --> 33:29.507
[Jingyeong chuckles]

33:30.050 --> 33:31.051
[chuckles]

33:31.426 --> 33:32.677
[chuckles]

33:34.804 --> 33:38.808
If you received a favor,
just repay them exactly what you owe.

33:38.892 --> 33:40.810
I think anything beyond that is excessive.

33:42.395 --> 33:44.022
You know,

33:45.023 --> 33:47.901
you act all high and mighty,
but you're a bit of a fool.

33:48.777 --> 33:52.280
I guess I don't really know
how much you owe them,

33:52.364 --> 33:55.909
but haven't you worked hard enough
that it's all been paid off?

33:56.409 --> 33:58.203
Then you don't need to do any more.

33:58.286 --> 33:59.746
In my opinion,

34:00.705 --> 34:03.416
compared to your boss,
the one who pretended to be ill,

34:03.500 --> 34:07.003
you're a hundred,
a thousand times smarter.

34:07.545 --> 34:10.382
So, you don't need
to keep putting up with it.

34:10.465 --> 34:11.716
Actually,

34:12.467 --> 34:13.718
you've got what it takes.

34:14.261 --> 34:16.763
The way I see it, you're quite all right.

34:18.265 --> 34:20.517
What, do you want me
to find you another job?

34:20.600 --> 34:21.768
[chuckles softly]

34:22.727 --> 34:23.812
[inhales deeply]

34:51.881 --> 34:52.924
INVESTMENT CONTRACT

35:08.356 --> 35:09.566
Article 8, Clause 3.

35:10.692 --> 35:13.153
Instead of paying the penalty for breach,

35:13.737 --> 35:16.448
it says BQ Capital can take part
in management.

35:16.531 --> 35:18.450
That's the clause you should point out.

35:18.533 --> 35:22.037
So, the justification is
to speed up the investment rounds?

35:22.120 --> 35:24.080
With the penalty,
it's about 60 billion won.

35:24.164 --> 35:26.374
That's about a 35-percent stake.

35:26.458 --> 35:27.917
With that, we can change bylaws,

35:28.001 --> 35:30.670
appoint directors,
or approve mergers and acquisitions.

35:32.339 --> 35:35.759
Once we take management control,
I'm going to sell the company in pieces.

35:37.636 --> 35:38.637
[in English] Okay.

35:41.973 --> 35:44.392
[in Korean] Before all that,
there's something

35:45.143 --> 35:46.811
I want to confirm with you.

35:47.520 --> 35:48.605
[chuckles softly]

36:06.331 --> 36:07.874
MUTUAL DIVORCE CONFIRMATION FORM

36:07.957 --> 36:09.167
APPLICANT JANG HANGU

36:09.751 --> 36:10.752
[chuckles softly]

36:10.835 --> 36:12.420
[♪ gripping, tense music playing]

36:19.427 --> 36:20.637
[Hangu chuckles softly]

36:22.889 --> 36:24.182
[gulps, sighs]

36:26.601 --> 36:27.727
[sighs in relief]

36:32.107 --> 36:33.900
HUSBAND JANG HANGU

36:44.911 --> 36:46.162
[sighs wearily]

36:46.663 --> 36:49.165
I can't get any work done
with all this chaos.

36:49.708 --> 36:51.876
[sighs wearily]
Tell me about it.

36:51.960 --> 36:53.503
I'D LIKE TO LEAVE THE SHOW...

36:53.586 --> 36:54.671
PRODUCER OF I AM SINGLE

36:54.754 --> 36:55.755
[Ms. Oh] What will you do?

36:56.756 --> 36:59.175
-Pardon?
-The company is about to be sold off.

36:59.259 --> 37:00.510
There's no time to relax.

37:02.470 --> 37:03.555
[sighs]

37:03.638 --> 37:05.890
That's why I withdrew.

37:06.266 --> 37:07.267
Withdrew from what?

37:07.934 --> 37:10.562
I feel like people will just talk
if I'm on the show.

37:10.937 --> 37:12.856
I just texted them that I'm stepping down

37:12.939 --> 37:15.066
from the show due to personal reasons.

37:15.150 --> 37:17.402
I wasn't asking you about I Am Single.

37:18.027 --> 37:20.447
There's a rumor going around

37:20.530 --> 37:22.907
that BQ Capital
will be running our company.

37:22.991 --> 37:24.451
Oh, that.

37:25.034 --> 37:26.119
[scoffs]

37:26.202 --> 37:27.954
I believe in our company.

37:28.037 --> 37:31.124
If it was going to fall just like this,
I wouldn't have worked here.

37:31.207 --> 37:33.626
Actually, me too.

37:33.710 --> 37:35.003
We're on the same page.

37:36.337 --> 37:37.464
[groans softly]

37:37.547 --> 37:39.257
[sighing] So naive.

37:39.716 --> 37:42.427
Start writing up a new resume.

37:42.510 --> 37:44.763
You should move while you're still young.

37:44.846 --> 37:47.140
Once you're older,
not many places will hire you.

37:49.058 --> 37:53.354
[Ms. Oh] Of course, there will be layoffs
once the ownership changes.

37:53.438 --> 37:55.523
You should be looking for a job now.

37:55.607 --> 37:58.109
You haven't worked for five years.
Have some conscience.

37:58.693 --> 38:00.236
What? A house-husband?

38:00.320 --> 38:02.405
Hey, I'm the one who cooks,

38:02.489 --> 38:03.698
pays for our child,

38:03.782 --> 38:05.575
and nurses your mom, you jerk.

38:05.658 --> 38:06.993
Just hang up! Geez.

38:07.076 --> 38:08.161
[line disconnects]

38:09.162 --> 38:10.330
[sighs in exasperation]

38:11.623 --> 38:14.042
I might actually be laid off at this rate.

38:14.959 --> 38:15.960
What do I do?

38:16.628 --> 38:17.921
[♪ melancholy music playing]

38:19.631 --> 38:20.632
[sighs]

38:24.761 --> 38:26.137
[sighs in despair]

38:27.222 --> 38:28.598
EXPECTED BQ RESPONSE

38:29.808 --> 38:33.144
BQ NEGOTIATION RESPONSE PLAN

38:33.812 --> 38:35.313
MEASURES AGAINST MASS LAYOFFS

38:38.691 --> 38:40.568
It suddenly hit me

38:40.944 --> 38:44.739
that these people's future
all depends on this agreement.

38:45.532 --> 38:47.867
[sighs] I really need to do well.

38:50.662 --> 38:51.788
When Grandma was around,

38:51.871 --> 38:54.165
the weight of responsibility
didn't feel so heavy.

38:54.249 --> 38:55.708
Of course.

38:55.792 --> 38:57.961
Did you think you'd go down alone?

38:59.003 --> 39:00.922
It'll be the end for the employees,

39:01.005 --> 39:02.507
and for my company, too.

39:02.590 --> 39:05.009
Myungsoondang is a huge client for me.

39:05.969 --> 39:08.555
That's why I'm here.
To see if you're doing a good job.

39:11.266 --> 39:12.350
Do you know

39:13.059 --> 39:15.770
when I'm most excited
and when it's the hardest for me?

39:17.438 --> 39:18.857
The payday.

39:19.607 --> 39:20.775
I know,

39:21.192 --> 39:23.528
my company is small
with only one employee.

39:23.611 --> 39:25.029
[♪ poignant music playing]

39:25.113 --> 39:26.781
But when we have no work that month,

39:26.865 --> 39:30.243
the approaching payday is frightening.

39:31.703 --> 39:33.997
I feel like I live to pay my employee.

39:34.080 --> 39:35.248
Work-life balance?

39:35.331 --> 39:36.457
What's that?

39:37.792 --> 39:40.795
Even if I feel like I'm about to collapse
from working all night,

39:40.879 --> 39:43.047
after paying my employee on time,

39:43.131 --> 39:45.133
I feel so proud.

39:46.843 --> 39:49.095
It feels like
I'm keeping a promise to people

39:49.178 --> 39:50.889
who trusted me and worked with me.

39:53.474 --> 39:56.060
After feeling such responsibility,

39:57.478 --> 40:01.024
I think I've become an adult.

40:03.318 --> 40:04.527
I'll keep trying.

40:08.698 --> 40:09.741
[sighs softly]

40:11.117 --> 40:13.411
I hope it goes well
with the investor tomorrow.

40:14.287 --> 40:16.539
If you can't pay the penalty,

40:17.832 --> 40:20.209
they'll probably take over
management, right?

40:20.293 --> 40:21.294
Yes.

40:22.253 --> 40:24.464
They'll most likely begin with layoffs.

40:24.547 --> 40:25.632
So, I'm worried.

40:26.049 --> 40:27.967
I have to stop that at all costs.

40:28.051 --> 40:30.094
What's the CEO of BQ Capital like?

40:33.514 --> 40:34.641
Her name is Sylvia.

40:34.724 --> 40:36.059
She's a Korean American.

40:36.142 --> 40:38.227
But I don't know anything
apart from her name.

40:40.021 --> 40:41.022
This person...

40:42.565 --> 40:44.233
I've seen her somewhere.

40:46.527 --> 40:47.612
Oh, wait!

41:03.586 --> 41:04.837
Look at this.

41:05.421 --> 41:08.841
It's a photo from the farewell party
when Sori quit her restaurant.

41:09.842 --> 41:11.177
Isn't she the same person?

41:12.387 --> 41:13.638
[♪ tense music playing]

41:13.721 --> 41:14.806
[Kim Wooju] Who is she?

41:14.889 --> 41:17.308
[Meri] She's the owner of the restaurant.

41:17.392 --> 41:19.143
But her name is different.

41:19.227 --> 41:21.980
She said her name was Jessica, not Sylvia.

41:23.982 --> 41:25.108
Jessica?

41:25.525 --> 41:27.610
[John in English] Since the address
matches perfectly,

41:27.694 --> 41:30.780
I looked up if the owner
was the same person, and it was.

41:30.863 --> 41:32.281
Her name is Jessica.

41:33.825 --> 41:34.993
J Consulting America
COMPANY FINANCIALS

41:35.076 --> 41:36.577
CEO Jessica

41:37.704 --> 41:40.248
[Meri] Do you think she's a twin?

41:44.419 --> 41:45.837
MERI

41:48.673 --> 41:49.966
What's this?

41:51.092 --> 41:53.052
-[phone vibrates]
-[Meri] Is this your boss?

41:56.014 --> 41:57.181
[Sori] Yes, it is.

41:57.598 --> 41:59.058
Where did you get this photo?

42:00.435 --> 42:01.477
[line connects]

42:02.353 --> 42:03.396
SORI

42:03.479 --> 42:05.189
[Meri] Take a closer look at the photo.

42:05.273 --> 42:06.399
She's called Sylvia.

42:06.482 --> 42:07.775
Are you sure it's your boss?

42:07.859 --> 42:09.235
[Sori] I told you it's her.

42:09.652 --> 42:11.779
-She's not a twin?
-She's not.

42:11.863 --> 42:13.656
That's her husband right next to her.

42:13.740 --> 42:15.658
[♪ tense, gripping music playing]

42:15.742 --> 42:16.743
Her husband?

42:17.368 --> 42:18.828
How do you know? You saw him?

42:18.911 --> 42:20.038
Yeah.

42:20.121 --> 42:22.623
I saw him when I dropped
her son off from school.

42:26.377 --> 42:28.087
[Hangu and Henry chuckle]

42:28.171 --> 42:29.464
He's heavy.

42:32.383 --> 42:33.426
I'm certain.

42:36.012 --> 42:37.305
[Meri] Okay.

42:37.972 --> 42:39.015
Bye.

42:44.645 --> 42:47.190
He's your uncle, isn't he?

42:48.483 --> 42:49.484
He is.

42:50.026 --> 42:53.112
What do you think is going on here?

42:53.196 --> 42:54.572
I think...

42:56.240 --> 42:58.117
Sylvia and Jessica

42:59.786 --> 43:01.120
are the same person.

43:03.331 --> 43:04.582
But then...

43:06.751 --> 43:07.919
that means...

43:09.921 --> 43:14.175
your uncle's working with the people
who are trying to take over the company.

43:15.551 --> 43:17.428
That's highly likely.

43:20.014 --> 43:22.391
If David was also in on it...

43:30.900 --> 43:34.612
Then, do you think
your aunt knows all this?

43:35.279 --> 43:37.031
That he even has a son in the US.

43:42.787 --> 43:44.580
MYUNGSOONDANG

43:50.461 --> 43:52.130
MUTUAL DIVORCE CONFIRMATION FORM

43:52.213 --> 43:53.673
APPLICANT JANG HANGU

43:54.298 --> 43:55.299
[sighs]

43:58.010 --> 43:59.220
What are you doing here?

43:59.303 --> 44:00.304
What? Nothing.

44:00.763 --> 44:01.848
What is it?

44:01.931 --> 44:04.267
I need to go to the hospital to see Mom.

44:04.350 --> 44:05.852
Can you drive?

44:05.935 --> 44:07.311
I'm too exhausted right now.

44:07.395 --> 44:09.272
Okay.

44:24.370 --> 44:26.205
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

44:39.051 --> 44:40.511
Welcome, ma'am.

44:41.554 --> 44:43.806
It's been a while. How have you been?

44:43.890 --> 44:46.017
As you know, the company's a bit...

44:46.809 --> 44:48.102
[Jessica] I'm sorry to hear it.

44:48.186 --> 44:50.813
Let's all put our heads together
and find a solution.

44:50.897 --> 44:52.356
Of course.

44:52.440 --> 44:54.775
These are our team leaders
joining us today.

44:54.859 --> 44:56.485
They're the chairwoman's grandsons.

44:57.195 --> 44:59.655
I'm Sylvia Oh, the CEO of BQ Capital.

44:59.739 --> 45:00.823
[acknowledges]

45:01.908 --> 45:03.201
I'm Jang Eungsoo.

45:08.539 --> 45:09.832
I'm Kim Wooju.

45:13.628 --> 45:15.296
[♪ dramatic sting]

45:15.755 --> 45:16.756
[Hangu] Please sit.

45:27.892 --> 45:29.393
Employment security?

45:30.478 --> 45:31.562
[clicks tongue, scoffs]

45:31.979 --> 45:33.689
I think you're mistaken.

45:34.941 --> 45:36.901
We're not running a charity.

45:36.984 --> 45:38.069
We're investors.

45:38.152 --> 45:39.195
However,

45:39.695 --> 45:42.698
from factory workers
to delivery drivers and café staff.

45:42.782 --> 45:44.909
They're all full-time employees
at Myungsoondang.

45:44.992 --> 45:46.744
-So, layoffs can't be--
-If you can't,

45:46.827 --> 45:48.246
pay the penalty.

45:50.539 --> 45:51.540
[Eungsoo] Ma'am.

45:51.624 --> 45:54.585
[chuckles softly]
Please don't be so harsh.

45:54.669 --> 45:57.922
If you could give us a little time,
we'll come up with a solution.

45:58.005 --> 45:59.048
[Jessica chuckles softly]

45:59.882 --> 46:02.677
Sales are tanking
with public opinion turning sour,

46:02.760 --> 46:05.137
and your assets
are all tied up in real estate.

46:05.221 --> 46:07.515
I also heard you can't
get any extra loans.

46:08.266 --> 46:09.600
Isn't that right?

46:09.684 --> 46:11.060
So, what can you do?

46:12.937 --> 46:15.064
If you want to recover
at least the investment,

46:15.147 --> 46:17.275
you'll even have to sell
the company in pieces.

46:18.859 --> 46:19.902
Is that what you want?

46:19.986 --> 46:21.028
Ma'am...

46:21.112 --> 46:22.655
[♪ ominous music playing]

46:26.409 --> 46:27.493
[sighs softly]

46:28.577 --> 46:29.787
Okay.

46:32.415 --> 46:36.669
We'll first discuss among ourselves
regarding your requests.

46:43.759 --> 46:45.136
CFO
JANG HANGU

46:45.219 --> 46:47.388
How could you be so emotional?

46:47.471 --> 46:49.515
Nothing good will come from crossing her.

46:51.183 --> 46:52.310
But...

46:53.561 --> 46:55.813
[Meri] Let's see how your uncle reacts.

46:56.272 --> 46:58.107
Then we can plan our strategy.

46:59.483 --> 47:00.526
I'm sorry.

47:01.152 --> 47:02.403
It was too unreasonable.

47:03.195 --> 47:04.947
[sighs] I know.

47:05.406 --> 47:07.366
But this isn't the time for it.

47:07.450 --> 47:08.701
Then,

47:09.744 --> 47:11.162
what do you think we should do?

47:12.496 --> 47:13.497
[sighs]

47:14.832 --> 47:16.959
We'll just have to give in to her demands.

47:17.835 --> 47:20.338
We should start
by laying off all management levels,

47:20.421 --> 47:22.214
and quickly sell off the factories

47:22.715 --> 47:24.467
and other real estate to secure cash.

47:25.718 --> 47:26.969
It'll be quite a loss, but...

47:38.314 --> 47:39.565
It's as we expected.

47:40.816 --> 47:42.360
They pretended to be strangers.

47:42.860 --> 47:44.445
They're trying to sell it off dirt cheap

47:44.528 --> 47:46.197
and turn it into an empty shell.

47:46.989 --> 47:49.909
Then they'll sell
the proprietary technology and the brand.

47:50.368 --> 47:51.410
This is frustrating.

47:51.494 --> 47:53.287
Can't we just expose them?

47:53.371 --> 47:55.498
Let everyone know about their affair

47:55.581 --> 47:56.999
and their plan for take over.

47:57.083 --> 48:00.669
But adultery can't be used
as decisive evidence.

48:01.379 --> 48:04.673
We need concrete proof
that they conspired to commit fraud.

48:05.758 --> 48:08.886
We can't access their phones or accounts
by reporting their adultery.

48:08.969 --> 48:11.305
And if they insist
they're unrelated work-wise,

48:11.389 --> 48:12.681
it won't get us anywhere.

48:13.682 --> 48:15.851
[inhales deeply, exhales]

48:17.645 --> 48:19.980
I wish the chairwoman
would regain her consciousness.

48:22.108 --> 48:23.150
[sighs]

48:25.027 --> 48:26.529
[heart monitor beeps steadily]

48:30.699 --> 48:31.826
[Miyeon] Mom.

48:32.827 --> 48:35.037
Please wake up.

48:35.996 --> 48:39.041
[crying] Wake up
so that I can tell you I'm sorry.

48:40.000 --> 48:43.504
Why do you always make me the bad person?

48:44.755 --> 48:45.840
[sniffles]

48:48.801 --> 48:51.178
Mom, please wake up.

48:52.638 --> 48:53.806
[sniffling]

48:53.889 --> 48:55.975
[sobbing] I'm sorry.

48:56.559 --> 48:58.227
Wake up.

49:02.189 --> 49:03.607
[Miyeon continues sobbing]

49:06.026 --> 49:07.027
What?

49:07.695 --> 49:09.280
Grandma woke up?

49:09.363 --> 49:10.865
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

49:12.575 --> 49:13.617
[sighs softly]

49:14.118 --> 49:15.453
Okay, Mom.

49:15.536 --> 49:17.455
I'll head to the hospital now.

49:19.081 --> 49:20.166
[elevator chimes]

49:31.510 --> 49:32.761
[Jessica] One, two, three.

49:33.262 --> 49:34.388
Mine.

49:34.930 --> 49:35.931
[chuckles]

49:36.515 --> 49:38.058
[in English] It's my turn, Mommy.

49:40.936 --> 49:42.188
One, two. [gasps]

49:42.271 --> 49:43.314
You took two?

49:43.397 --> 49:45.274
My turn. Watch.

49:45.357 --> 49:46.442
One...

49:46.525 --> 49:47.568
Hold on.

49:49.445 --> 49:50.446
Hello?

49:54.158 --> 49:55.493
She woke up?

49:57.369 --> 49:58.454
[sighs softly]

49:58.537 --> 50:00.206
[♪ ominous music playing]

50:06.253 --> 50:07.296
VIP
KO PHILNYUN

50:41.997 --> 50:43.666
[Hangu] That old hag knows everything.

50:43.749 --> 50:45.125
We need to get rid of her now.

50:59.557 --> 51:01.058
[♪ music increases in tempo]

51:14.405 --> 51:15.948
-[gasps, yelps]
-[grunts]

51:17.116 --> 51:18.117
[grunts] Let me go!

51:18.659 --> 51:19.702
[grunts]

51:20.286 --> 51:21.328
[grunts, gasps]

51:21.620 --> 51:22.663
[panting]

51:25.332 --> 51:26.875
[yelps]

51:27.293 --> 51:28.419
[screams, grunts]

51:29.253 --> 51:30.754
[grunting] Let me go!

51:32.298 --> 51:34.967
-[yelps]
-[both panting]

51:35.050 --> 51:36.051
Oh Minjeong.

51:36.135 --> 51:37.136
[panting]

51:38.053 --> 51:39.430
[both grunting]

51:40.931 --> 51:41.932
[Jessica] No...

51:42.308 --> 51:43.726
No.

51:43.809 --> 51:44.935
Ms. Oh Minjeong.

51:45.019 --> 51:47.438
-You're under arrest for attempted murder.
-No.

51:47.521 --> 51:49.189
-No.
-You have the right to remain silent,

51:49.273 --> 51:50.441
the right to an attorney,

51:50.524 --> 51:52.735
and the right to request
a review of your arrest.

51:52.818 --> 51:54.278
-[Jessica] No!
-[officer] Take her away.

51:54.361 --> 51:55.821
[Jessica grunts, yelps]

51:57.072 --> 51:58.282
Let me go, damn it.

51:59.074 --> 52:00.075
Let go!

52:00.159 --> 52:01.827
[♪ music crescendos]

52:03.621 --> 52:04.913
It hurts.

52:13.380 --> 52:16.133
[Kim Wooju] We can't access their phones
or accounts by reporting them.

52:16.216 --> 52:18.218
And if they insist
they're unrelated to work,

52:18.302 --> 52:19.303
it'd be no use.

52:20.012 --> 52:22.389
I wish the chairwoman
would regain her consciousness.

52:23.015 --> 52:24.016
[sighs]

52:26.685 --> 52:27.686
[gasps softly]

52:28.646 --> 52:31.774
Let's make her wake up.

52:32.775 --> 52:34.818
Then the guilty one will come forward,

52:34.902 --> 52:36.820
the one who's afraid of her waking up.

52:37.571 --> 52:39.698
Catch that person

52:39.782 --> 52:41.742
to get access
to their phones and accounts.

52:43.160 --> 52:45.829
To do that, we need help from this person.

52:48.207 --> 52:49.667
[Eungsoo] What? Sylvia Oh?

52:50.459 --> 52:52.586
[Kim Wooju] I'm sorry to tell you this,

52:52.670 --> 52:55.130
but I'm sure of the relationship
between her and Uncle.

52:55.214 --> 52:58.008
And that woman is also related
to J Consulting in the US--

52:58.092 --> 52:59.343
Stop there.

52:59.760 --> 53:00.803
You knew?

53:03.347 --> 53:04.473
[sighs softly]

53:04.556 --> 53:07.643
I already knew Dad had a woman.

53:08.018 --> 53:09.645
I also knew that she was in the US.

53:09.728 --> 53:10.771
But... [sighs]

53:11.605 --> 53:13.190
I didn't know that was Sylvia Oh.

53:18.821 --> 53:20.948
I'm sure this is a lot to take in.

53:22.908 --> 53:24.076
There's another problem.

53:25.661 --> 53:28.706
Uncle and that woman
are planning to sell the company.

53:28.789 --> 53:30.207
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

53:31.625 --> 53:34.336
But you don't have any proof.
This is just your guess.

53:34.420 --> 53:36.922
Exactly, and I need your help
to find proof.

53:37.589 --> 53:39.591
To protect Grandma, the company,

53:40.467 --> 53:42.261
and even Auntie...

53:47.224 --> 53:48.767
[sighs] What do I have to do?

53:50.853 --> 53:52.521
[♪ stealthy music playing]

54:01.405 --> 54:02.573
What?

54:03.157 --> 54:04.742
Grandma woke up?

54:06.910 --> 54:07.911
[elevator button beeps]

54:08.287 --> 54:09.329
[sighs softly]

54:10.038 --> 54:11.206
Okay, Mom.

54:11.290 --> 54:13.333
I'll head to the hospital now.

54:14.293 --> 54:15.377
[elevator chimes]

54:20.674 --> 54:21.675
[sighs wearily]

54:24.720 --> 54:26.180
[♪ music crescendos, fades]

54:35.689 --> 54:36.774
Watch her head.

54:36.857 --> 54:40.486
[Meri] Ms. Oh Minjeong came,
not Director Jang.

54:40.944 --> 54:43.155
[Kim Wooju] Someone's been caught,
and it's just the start.

54:44.156 --> 54:47.493
Once they investigate her,
they'll find out who she's involved with.

54:49.536 --> 54:51.163
[siren wailing]

54:58.462 --> 54:59.713
Good work.

55:01.048 --> 55:02.591
I'm sure it was tough for you.

55:04.927 --> 55:06.386
You did well, too.

55:08.055 --> 55:09.348
Aren't you hungry?

55:09.431 --> 55:10.891
Do you want to go eat something?

55:11.767 --> 55:12.768
Sure.

55:16.438 --> 55:18.023
What do you want to eat?

55:18.357 --> 55:19.650
[hums thoughtfully]

55:21.443 --> 55:23.111
-Spicy stir-fried pork?
-[chuckles]

55:24.613 --> 55:27.491
At a hospital in Seoul,
BQ Capital CEO, Oh Minjeong,

55:27.574 --> 55:28.992
was arrested for attempting

55:29.076 --> 55:31.328
to poison Myungsoondang's chairwoman
Ko Philnyun.

55:31.411 --> 55:34.164
According to the police,
early yesterday morning,

55:34.248 --> 55:37.543
Ms. Oh infiltrated the chairwoman's
VIP hospital room,

55:37.626 --> 55:39.628
in an attempt to drug her.

55:39.711 --> 55:41.088
[reporter 1] With the forged contract,

55:41.171 --> 55:43.590
Myungsoondang was accused
of investment fraud.

55:43.674 --> 55:45.008
But the police has confirmed

55:45.092 --> 55:47.177
that Myungsoondang
was essentially the victim.

55:47.261 --> 55:49.638
[reporter 2] Police found evidence
from Ms. Oh's phone and emails

55:49.721 --> 55:53.350
indicating that she conspired
with a former executive of the Kaltz Hotel

55:53.433 --> 55:55.894
to forge the contract
and carry out the fraud.

55:55.978 --> 55:57.980
The police are now
cooperating with Interpol...

55:58.063 --> 56:00.399
I've told them already.

56:00.482 --> 56:03.026
I told them the chairwoman
would never do such a thing.

56:03.110 --> 56:05.696
But young people these days
aren't loyal to the company.

56:05.779 --> 56:08.115
They tried to send in resumes
to other companies,

56:08.198 --> 56:09.366
so I gave them an earful.

56:09.908 --> 56:13.787
I told them they shouldn't be
so disloyal to the company.

56:13.870 --> 56:14.871
[chuckles awkwardly]

56:17.332 --> 56:18.625
Oh, hey, guys. [chuckles]

56:19.001 --> 56:20.419
When did they get here?

56:20.502 --> 56:21.587
Ms. Oh...

56:22.296 --> 56:23.797
What a traitor.

56:23.880 --> 56:26.383
-Do you know how hard--
-We can do this!

56:26.466 --> 56:28.218
Let's work hard. Let's go!

56:31.597 --> 56:32.639
[Wonseok clears throat]

56:35.475 --> 56:36.476
Thank you, all of you.

56:37.769 --> 56:39.187
For believing in the company.

56:39.813 --> 56:43.066
I think we were able to get through
this crisis thanks to you.

56:43.150 --> 56:47.029
I'm sure you had it the toughest, Mr. Kim.
[chuckles softly]

56:48.280 --> 56:49.823
What's happening now, then?

56:49.906 --> 56:52.868
I heard a rumor
that Director Jang was involved.

56:53.785 --> 56:56.079
Sejung, I told you that was a secret.

56:57.205 --> 56:58.290
[whispers] Was it a secret?

56:58.373 --> 56:59.791
[Wonseok whispers] Didn't I tell you?

56:59.875 --> 57:02.044
[Sejung] I thought everyone
on the team knew.

57:03.086 --> 57:04.171
[phone vibrating]

57:04.921 --> 57:07.466
JUNGMUN POLICE STATION, DETECTIVE PARK

57:08.759 --> 57:10.844
[Det. Park] From the forensic analysis
of Ms. Oh's phone,

57:10.927 --> 57:13.221
we found evidence
that she conspired with David.

57:14.556 --> 57:18.060
But there were no personal texts
between her and Mr. Jang Hangu.

57:18.477 --> 57:20.979
There were also
no transactions to Mr. Jang's account.

57:22.064 --> 57:23.065
Really?

57:24.483 --> 57:26.610
She doesn't know anyone in Seoul,

57:26.693 --> 57:28.362
I had no choice but to come.

57:32.491 --> 57:33.950
[sighs, clicks tongue]

57:34.034 --> 57:35.744
It's not like you did anything wrong.

57:36.870 --> 57:37.996
Eat slowly.

57:38.080 --> 57:39.164
Okay.

57:39.831 --> 57:40.999
[in English] It's so yummy.

57:41.083 --> 57:42.084
[laughs]

57:43.794 --> 57:45.837
Put that down when you're eating.

57:46.338 --> 57:47.422
No.

57:47.506 --> 57:48.715
[in Korean] No.

57:49.132 --> 57:51.093
He's eating with me.

57:52.594 --> 57:53.762
Fine.

57:54.805 --> 57:57.265
I guess eating alone can get lonely.

57:57.724 --> 57:59.101
-Eat together then.
-[giggles]

57:59.935 --> 58:01.520
[in English] You want to eat some, too?

58:05.649 --> 58:09.444
I asked a restaurant manager
I used to work with to look after him.

58:10.404 --> 58:12.739
I only asked her
to help me out for a few days.

58:12.823 --> 58:14.324
So, please look after Henry.

58:14.408 --> 58:15.826
Don't worry.

58:17.327 --> 58:19.830
You deleted all the records
from the server, right?

58:21.164 --> 58:22.165
Yes.

58:23.166 --> 58:25.961
I also got rid of the phone
that I used to contact you.

58:27.045 --> 58:28.422
You did great. [chuckles]

58:29.339 --> 58:31.216
Someone's got to look after Henry.

58:31.925 --> 58:33.427
What did the lawyer say?

58:34.219 --> 58:36.680
They said you'll get about 15 years.

58:36.763 --> 58:39.641
But I'll use the best lawyer
to get you out as soon as possible.

58:43.770 --> 58:47.357
All you need to do is just remain silent.

58:48.150 --> 58:49.317
You'll get a divorce

58:50.444 --> 58:52.988
and take Henry to the US, right?

58:54.573 --> 58:55.782
[♪ tense music playing]

58:56.283 --> 58:57.284
Of course.

58:59.035 --> 59:00.036
Don't worry.

59:02.289 --> 59:04.666
[♪ dramatic sting, music fades]

59:20.974 --> 59:23.393
What brings you by without calling ahead?

59:23.477 --> 59:24.936
Are you coming from somewhere?

59:25.020 --> 59:27.397
Oh, I had a meeting outside.

59:27.481 --> 59:29.900
Not from a meeting
with Ms. Oh Minjeong, are you?

59:29.983 --> 59:31.359
[♪ gripping, tense music playing]

59:35.947 --> 59:36.948
What are you saying?

59:37.449 --> 59:39.910
I know of your relationship.

59:41.328 --> 59:42.412
That you lied to us

59:42.496 --> 59:45.207
to embezzle company funds
through J Consulting.

59:46.416 --> 59:47.417
[scoffs softly]

59:48.043 --> 59:49.669
And that you have a son in the US.

59:51.630 --> 59:52.839
Uncle,

59:53.298 --> 59:55.550
I'll expose everything

59:55.634 --> 59:58.512
that you've conspired
with Ms. Oh Minjeong.

01:00:01.515 --> 01:00:02.974
I was blackmailed.

01:00:05.852 --> 01:00:07.521
I had no choice.

01:00:08.146 --> 01:00:10.398
I was being dragged around by her threats.

01:00:10.482 --> 01:00:13.485
She said she wouldn't just sit back
if I didn't get the money.

01:00:13.568 --> 01:00:16.530
She also said the child is mine,
but I'm not really sure.

01:00:17.656 --> 01:00:18.824
I'm also scared.

01:00:21.493 --> 01:00:22.536
Believe me.

01:00:23.286 --> 01:00:25.747
Aside from the private contract
with J Consulting,

01:00:26.456 --> 01:00:29.209
I had nothing to do with BQ Capital.

01:00:29.292 --> 01:00:30.961
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:00:35.966 --> 01:00:36.967
[Eungsoo scoffs]

01:00:37.968 --> 01:00:38.969
Is that what he said?

01:00:40.846 --> 01:00:41.847
Yes.

01:00:44.182 --> 01:00:45.267
[sighs in exasperation]

01:00:45.976 --> 01:00:46.977
[scoffs]

01:00:50.730 --> 01:00:51.857
[sighs wearily]

01:00:59.865 --> 01:01:01.950
I'm not sure if this would help,

01:01:02.409 --> 01:01:03.743
but it'd at least prove

01:01:03.827 --> 01:01:06.037
that their relationship
wasn't based on a threat.

01:01:06.538 --> 01:01:08.373
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

01:01:13.962 --> 01:01:16.715
[Eungsoo] Back when I was 20,
on my way back home,

01:01:16.798 --> 01:01:19.467
I saw Dad secretly being
on the phone in the car.

01:01:19.551 --> 01:01:22.554
He was on the phone
every night in secret for hours.

01:01:23.346 --> 01:01:25.140
I wondered what it was about.

01:01:25.515 --> 01:01:27.434
So, I listened to the dash cam recordings.

01:01:29.269 --> 01:01:31.855
[Hangu] I'm going to New York next week
regarding Wooju's school.

01:01:31.938 --> 01:01:33.356
It's a tight schedule,

01:01:33.440 --> 01:01:35.400
so why don't you come to New York?

01:01:36.151 --> 01:01:37.152
[mouse clicks]

01:01:37.986 --> 01:01:39.029
Are you mad?

01:01:39.446 --> 01:01:42.407
I'll reserve your favorite restaurant
in New York.

01:01:43.241 --> 01:01:44.326
I miss you, too.

01:01:45.702 --> 01:01:47.120
[♪ tense music playing]

01:01:49.039 --> 01:01:50.081
[sighs softly]

01:01:50.165 --> 01:01:52.500
This isn't enough to prove embezzlement

01:01:53.001 --> 01:01:55.670
and the attempted murder of my grandma.

01:01:59.799 --> 01:02:00.926
[sighs wearily]

01:02:32.040 --> 01:02:35.585
Why did you try to kill Grandma?

01:02:41.883 --> 01:02:43.093
Should I tell you?

01:02:45.053 --> 01:02:47.347
Even without killing her,

01:02:48.056 --> 01:02:50.600
you could legally take over Myungsoondang.

01:02:51.851 --> 01:02:54.521
But why did you try to murder her?

01:02:59.234 --> 01:03:00.402
Perhaps Grandma knew

01:03:01.319 --> 01:03:04.781
that you and Jang Hangu
conspired together.

01:03:10.078 --> 01:03:11.121
I...

01:03:12.247 --> 01:03:13.790
I don't know

01:03:14.916 --> 01:03:16.710
Jang Hangu personally.

01:03:17.168 --> 01:03:18.420
Ms. Oh.

01:03:20.171 --> 01:03:22.173
I think you're trying to take the fall.

01:03:23.216 --> 01:03:25.510
But do you think Jang Hangu
will keep his promise?

01:03:29.889 --> 01:03:31.349
[Hangu] I had no choice.

01:03:31.808 --> 01:03:33.768
I was being dragged around by her threats.

01:03:33.852 --> 01:03:36.229
She wouldn't just sit back
if I didn't get the money.

01:03:36.312 --> 01:03:39.357
She also said the child is mine,
but I'm not really sure.

01:03:39.733 --> 01:03:40.900
I'm also scared.

01:03:40.984 --> 01:03:42.444
[♪ tense, dramatic music playing]

01:03:43.570 --> 01:03:46.865
Jang Hangu is already trying
to abandon you and your child.

01:03:49.492 --> 01:03:50.744
So, think carefully

01:03:51.411 --> 01:03:53.038
if you want to protect your son.

01:03:56.416 --> 01:03:57.500
[Jessica] Promise me...

01:04:00.295 --> 01:04:01.880
Henry's safety.

01:04:02.756 --> 01:04:04.007
[breath trembling]

01:04:04.090 --> 01:04:05.216
Then,

01:04:06.593 --> 01:04:08.011
I'll give you what you want.

01:04:08.636 --> 01:04:09.763
[sighs softly]

01:04:16.019 --> 01:04:18.021
The proof that you conspired
with Jang Hangu.

01:04:19.814 --> 01:04:20.815
Where is it?

01:04:21.941 --> 01:04:23.109
[breath trembling]

01:04:27.572 --> 01:04:29.157
CFO
JANG HANGU

01:04:29.949 --> 01:04:32.660
[Jessica] Just because I got rid
of the server and the phone,

01:04:32.744 --> 01:04:33.870
don't think you're safe.

01:04:34.913 --> 01:04:36.414
Because that's not everything.

01:04:37.373 --> 01:04:38.750
Don't forget.

01:04:38.833 --> 01:04:41.461
We got on the same boat 25 years ago,

01:04:41.544 --> 01:04:45.590
and neither of us can get off it first.

01:04:48.718 --> 01:04:50.845
"That's not everything..."

01:04:50.929 --> 01:04:52.639
[♪ music increases in tempo]

01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:06.945
[bag unzips]

01:05:07.028 --> 01:05:08.363
[♪ ominous music playing]

01:05:23.711 --> 01:05:25.004
[exclaims in annoyance]

01:05:31.136 --> 01:05:32.137
[grunts]

01:05:36.766 --> 01:05:37.934
[exclaims in frustration]

01:05:43.940 --> 01:05:45.108
[panting]

01:05:55.285 --> 01:05:56.536
[♪ music crescendos]

01:06:01.166 --> 01:06:02.542
[Henry in English] Mommy, wait.

01:06:06.171 --> 01:06:08.006
[chuckles] Look at him.

01:06:08.464 --> 01:06:11.426
He always takes that with him
because it's a gift from you.

01:06:11.843 --> 01:06:12.844
[chuckles]

01:06:25.607 --> 01:06:26.649
[object clicks]

01:06:28.401 --> 01:06:29.777
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

01:06:41.331 --> 01:06:42.874
[♪ music increases in tempo]

01:06:45.627 --> 01:06:46.711
[scoffs]

01:06:51.591 --> 01:06:52.592
[sighs softly]

01:06:55.011 --> 01:06:56.471
[cell phone powers on]

01:06:57.639 --> 01:06:59.599
[Hangu] You go ahead to Unit 401.

01:06:59.682 --> 01:07:01.267
I'll leave when my wife is asleep.

01:07:01.351 --> 01:07:02.685
My brother-in-law noticed.

01:07:02.769 --> 01:07:04.229
We'll have to be careful.

01:07:04.312 --> 01:07:05.813
Of course, I miss you, too.

01:07:05.897 --> 01:07:08.066
Just wait until everything is finished.

01:07:08.149 --> 01:07:09.317
Don't be anxious.

01:07:09.400 --> 01:07:10.818
Just trust me.

01:07:10.902 --> 01:07:12.654
Everything will go as planned.

01:07:15.240 --> 01:07:17.200
THEY JUST LEFT
PLATE NUMBER SEOUL 10 NI 3309

01:07:21.037 --> 01:07:22.080
They just left.

01:07:22.163 --> 01:07:24.499
25 YEARS AGO

01:07:24.582 --> 01:07:28.878
The plate number is Seoul 10 Ni 3309.

01:07:34.008 --> 01:07:35.051
[Miyeon] Honey.

01:07:36.803 --> 01:07:37.887
What are you doing?

01:07:37.971 --> 01:07:39.222
Come have some fruit.

01:07:39.305 --> 01:07:40.515
Okay, I'm on my way.

01:07:40.598 --> 01:07:41.891
[both chuckle]

01:07:41.975 --> 01:07:43.268
I looked everywhere for you.

01:07:45.687 --> 01:07:47.397
THEY JUST LEFT
PLATE: SEOUL 10 NI 3309

01:07:47.480 --> 01:07:48.940
[♪ tense, foreboding music continues]

01:07:52.193 --> 01:07:53.403
UNDER CONSTRUCTION
NO ENTRY

01:07:53.486 --> 01:07:54.696
NO ENTRY

01:08:02.787 --> 01:08:04.956
-There must be a construction site.
-I guess so.

01:08:06.708 --> 01:08:08.418
SEOUL 10 NI 3309

01:08:18.928 --> 01:08:20.346
Are you still upset, Wooju?

01:08:20.430 --> 01:08:24.851
It was my birthday present.
Why did you give it to Eungsoo?

01:08:24.934 --> 01:08:26.644
It was mine.

01:08:26.728 --> 01:08:28.938
He wanted it.

01:08:29.022 --> 01:08:31.733
His whole family came
to wish you a happy birthday.

01:08:31.816 --> 01:08:33.901
-Couldn't you give him that?
-No.

01:08:34.777 --> 01:08:37.864
He always takes what's mine.

01:08:38.489 --> 01:08:40.158
He's a mean pig.

01:08:40.241 --> 01:08:43.077
You can't talk like that
about your cousin.

01:08:43.161 --> 01:08:44.454
Take it back.

01:08:53.171 --> 01:08:54.630
Or Dad will get really angry.

01:08:55.089 --> 01:08:56.174
You won't take it back?

01:08:58.551 --> 01:09:01.554
You're a good boy, aren't you?
Do as your dad says.

01:09:02.680 --> 01:09:03.681
[exclaims]

01:09:04.432 --> 01:09:05.641
You won't take it back?

01:09:06.517 --> 01:09:07.894
[Kim Wooju's dad sighs]

01:09:08.186 --> 01:09:11.814
Then I won't buy you the toy robot.

01:09:19.697 --> 01:09:20.740
[gasps] Honey!

01:09:20.823 --> 01:09:22.033
[truck horn blaring]

01:09:23.201 --> 01:09:24.869
-[all scream]
-[horn blaring]

01:09:24.952 --> 01:09:26.829
[tires screeching]

01:09:39.384 --> 01:09:40.802
[♪ ominous music playing]

01:09:51.437 --> 01:09:53.689
I TOOK CARE OF IT

01:09:58.861 --> 01:10:00.738
[exclaims smugly] This was it.

01:10:11.332 --> 01:10:12.500
-[sighs softly]
-[laptop chimes]

01:10:14.001 --> 01:10:16.254
PHONE RECORDINGS

01:10:16.337 --> 01:10:17.797
[♪ music increases in tempo]

01:10:29.016 --> 01:10:32.019
[Jessica] The president
found out about us.

01:10:32.478 --> 01:10:33.521
What do we do?

01:10:33.604 --> 01:10:34.939
[Hangu] We need to get rid of him.

01:10:35.022 --> 01:10:36.023
[Jessica] What?

01:10:36.107 --> 01:10:38.401
[Hangu] There's a family gathering
in Yeosu next week.

01:10:38.484 --> 01:10:41.571
That's when we'll have to get it done.

01:10:53.082 --> 01:10:54.083
[whistling tune]

01:10:55.001 --> 01:10:56.335
[♪ dramatic sting]

01:11:17.565 --> 01:11:18.733
Was it you, Uncle?

01:11:22.653 --> 01:11:23.654
Tell me.

01:11:25.823 --> 01:11:27.033
Was it you?

01:11:27.116 --> 01:11:28.493
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

01:11:37.627 --> 01:11:38.711
[♪ ethereal sparkle]

01:11:38.795 --> 01:11:40.338
[♪ dreamy pop music playing]

01:11:47.178 --> 01:11:49.806
THANKS TO KIM MINSANG
FOR THE SPECIAL APPEARANCE

01:12:05.279 --> 01:12:07.949
WOULD YOU MARRY ME?

01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:09.575
[Kim Wooju] He asked me for forgiveness,

01:12:09.659 --> 01:12:10.785
but he killed my parents.

01:12:10.868 --> 01:12:12.912
[judge] The nature
of the crime is heinous,

01:12:12.995 --> 01:12:14.580
-and its social harm is substantial.
-[Hangu screaming]

01:12:14.664 --> 01:12:17.375
Accordingly, this court hereby
grants the defendant...

01:12:17.458 --> 01:12:19.001
[Jingyeong] She regained
her consciousness.

01:12:19.085 --> 01:12:20.670
[Meri] Let's meet at home.

01:12:20.753 --> 01:12:24.048
I don't think we can accept
the house that I won through the raffle.

01:12:24.131 --> 01:12:26.592
Well, this really feels
like we're newlyweds.

01:12:26.676 --> 01:12:27.760
[Kim Wooju] We are newlyweds.

01:12:27.844 --> 01:12:29.679
-My heart...
-[Sejung] Let's buy some fruit.

01:12:29.762 --> 01:12:31.472
[Eunsook] Didn't you know
she's a divorcée?

01:12:31.556 --> 01:12:33.850
-[Youngsook] Let's end this together!
-[Wooju's sister] No, stop!

01:12:33.933 --> 01:12:35.142
[Sori screams]

01:12:35.226 --> 01:12:36.519
[Jingyeong] Why don't you call me

01:12:37.019 --> 01:12:38.020
once a week?

01:12:38.855 --> 01:12:40.106
[Wooju] Just wait.

01:12:40.189 --> 01:12:41.482
I'm still here.

01:12:41.566 --> 01:12:42.859
[Meri] Something happened, Wooju.

01:12:42.942 --> 01:12:44.610
A woman, my current legal wife,

01:12:44.694 --> 01:12:45.736
Yoo Meri.

01:12:45.862 --> 01:12:46.946
[Kim Wooju] What?

01:12:47.029 --> 01:12:48.114
A press conference?

01:12:50.616 --> 01:12:52.618
Translated by Susanna Kim
